{
  "name": "permissions-det (the Authorizations screen against the seeded governance.db: the rules for every agent and of one agent, a withdrawal and its undo, revoke all never confirmed, the load error, the agent sheet, then developer mode: add, duplicate, edit)",
  "stopOnError": false,
  "notes": [
    "The settings hold no permissions section: the rules live on the Authorizations screen, a route of its own (authorizations), which the recipe opens directly.",
    "A withdrawal takes effect at once and asks no confirmation; the line stays in place with its undo (authorizations-rule-undo writes the rule again, authorizations-always-undo gives the consent back). The recipe withdraws and undoes one standing consent of apollia:chat, then the first fine rule for every agent, so the seeded counts are the same after the run, the rule with a new id. No agent of the seed holds a fine rule of its own after the access upgrade, so the fine rule is played on the rules for every agent.",
    "authorizations-revoke-all-confirm is waited for and never clicked; destructive.json confirms it.",
    "The load error is produced by a once-stub that rejects governance_list_permission_rules; the screen loads on mount, so the recipe leaves for the policy screen and comes back to mount it again, twice: once into the error, once out of it.",
    "The effect and the scope of a rule are RadioItem buttons, not <select>: they are clicked. The family, the tool and the agent are native <select>, driven by selectOption.",
    "The standing consents (authorizations-always) come from the access upgrade the runtime runs once at startup (apollia-permissions access_upgrade.rs): the seed holds no row in family_consents, but its two Allow rules without a prefix, web_search for apollia:chat and file_edit for a project, become standing consents of the built-in agent, marked as carried over from an earlier version (AlwaysRow.svelte:40-41). The recipe asserts them on the screen and on the agent sheet, where the rows are the same AlwaysRow under agent-sheet-always (SheetAlways.svelte:66-84), and the empty states (authorizations-always-empty, agent-sheet-always-empty) are asserted absent."
  ],
